# Lumen design system — Cursor rules

> Mirror of [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md). If the file you're editing references Lumen tokens or components, these rules apply.

## Hard rules

1. **Never hardcode tokens.** Use semantic tokens (`var(--color-surface-page)`, `LumenTokens.text.primary`, etc.). Lint catches raw hex/px in component code.
2. **Use SEMANTIC tokens, not primitives.** `color.surface.default`, not `color.warm.50`.
3. **Component contracts (`component.json`) must validate against `/design-system/02-components/_schema/component.schema.json`.**
4. **Accessibility floor: WCAG 2.2 AA.** Visible focus, contrast, keyboard reachability, accessible name.
5. **Warp green (`accent.500` = `#4ade80`) plays one role only**: action / live / success. Never decorative.
6. **Honor `prefers-reduced-motion`.**

## Token quick reference

| Need | Token |
|---|---|
| Page canvas | `color.surface.page` |
| Card surface | `color.surface.raised` |
| Primary text | `color.text.primary` |
| Secondary text | `color.text.secondary` |
| Hairline border | `color.border.subtle` |
| Primary CTA bg | `color.action.primary.bg.rest` |
| Success bg/fg | `color.status.success.bg` / `.fg` |
| Default radius (cards) | `radius.card.default` |
| Default radius (buttons) | `radius.control.md` |
| Default UI motion | `motion.transition.base` |

## When generating Lumen UI code

- Web: Tailwind v4 utilities mapped to Lumen tokens via `@theme`. `bg-page`, `text-fg`, `rounded-lg`, etc.
- React Native: NativeWind with `@lumen/tokens-rn`.
- iOS: `LumenTokens.{layer}.{key}` from the Swift Package.
- Android: `LumenTokens.{Layer}.{key}` from the Compose object.

## Generation workflow

When asked to create a new UI piece:

1. Check `design-system/02-components/` for the closest existing component.
2. Compose using existing components.
3. If no fit exists, follow `_meta/prompts/new-component.md`.
4. Use the voice rules in `design-system/04-content/ui-writing-style.md` for any copy.
5. Cite token paths in inline comments where it adds clarity.

## When unsure

- Look at `audit-dashboard/src/` for working examples of every component pattern.
- Read the `component.md` of the closest match.
- Surface the question — don't guess.
